  "notes": "Hakka (Hak-kâ-ngî) romanised input contract: Pha̍k-fa-sṳ, the Hakka counterpart of Pe̍h-ōe-jī (Hashimoto 1973 for the underlying phonology, Meixian reference dialect). j/q/x spell the alveolo-palatal series distinct from z/c/s, earning their keys by test 1 (their IPA is not the concatenation of any Latin-letter parts in this alphabet). ii spells the apical/high-central vowel that only occurs after sibilant initials, earning its key by test 3: without it the tokenizer's maximal munch would try the plain i grapheme and miscall the vowel quality. Tone is lexical (6 citation tones); the stress schema does not apply (exemption, quality_tiers.md). No WikiPron gold exists in this romanisation (WikiPron's hak_hani file is Han-character keyed), so the tier stays at skeleton pending a Pha̍k-fa-sṳ gold source.",
